# cronwatcher.tab: like a crontab, but every script is hashed and verified before each run.
# Install as /etc/cronwatcher.tab, owned by root, not writable by group/others.
# Scripts are trusted when first seen; a changed script stays blocked until
# `cronwatcher approve <script>`. A script missing at startup stays pending until approved.
# Restart the service after editing this file (@reboot jobs still run only once per boot).
#
# m    h  dom mon dow  [user]  command [args...]  (absolute path, no shell: put pipes/quoting into the script)
# user: run as that account (its groups, HOME, cwd = home); root still verifies the script first.
#       Without it, the job runs as the daemon (root). Needs the daemon to run as root.
*/5    *  *   *   *    /opt/jobs/backup.sh --full
30     2  *   *   1-5  /opt/jobs/report.sh
5      5  *   *   *    alice  /home/alice/jobs/daily.sh
@daily                 /usr/local/bin/rotate-logs
@reboot                /opt/jobs/warmup.sh
# Runs (verified too) when any job is refused. Gets CRONWATCHER_TAMPERED and CRONWATCHER_REASON.
@tamper                /opt/jobs/alert.sh
